# deploy.ps1 compares these against the device BYTE FOR BYTE, so git must not
# rewrite their line endings. With core.autocrlf=true a checkout would convert
# them to CRLF and -Check would report a permanent false difference.
#
# The device genuinely has MIXED endings: code.py is LF, boot.py is CRLF, which
# is just how they were authored. Each file is pinned to the form actually on the
# board so the repo mirrors it exactly. Nothing here has been flashed — if the
# device is ever normalised, update these lines to match.
code.py          text eol=lf
test.py          text eol=lf
code.proposed.py text eol=lf
boot.py          text eol=crlf
